# Wave W17-X (Route 210): ranch pine — a paddock pine in warm pasture greens, tiered and sturdy, its highlight lifted clear of the turf, on ranch turf (ground baked in). Route 210’s own tree — split from Route 209’s sage bell pine by warmth and from its North segment’s frosted fog pine by register entire: this pine stands in clear herd weather, that one in murk.
